From 9be1d3dccfa623515c0f4a2bb8f40c7f4009b620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Nov 2025 12:54:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Implement PadAI Phase 1 MVP

Phase 1: FastAPI + React Flow with simple curl-based agent coordination

Backend:
- FastAPI server with HTTP endpoints (/api/status, /api/claim, /api/complete, /api/tasks)
- Python bd CLI wrapper (beads.py) for task operations
- CORS enabled for React frontend

Frontend:
- React + TypeScript + Vite
- React Flow visualization with Dagre layout
- Real-time status polling (5s interval)
- Dark theme UI with status color coding

Infrastructure:
- Dockerfile for containerized deployment
- Railway.json for one-click Railway deployment
- test-agent.sh script for workflow testing

Agent Workflow (curl):
1. GET /api/ready - list available tasks
2. POST /api/claim - claim next task
3. Do the work
4. POST /api/complete - mark as done

Tested:
- All API endpoints working
- Task claim/complete workflow verified
- Ready task parsing fixed for bd CLI output format
- Status aggregation from bd status command

Phase 2 roadmap:
- Remote MCP instead of curl
- Agent Mail integration
- WebSocket real-time updates
- Telegram bot
